   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1791431790027,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1. decided: the person signs each change, never the list\n\n2. must every question name a consumer before it is asked?\n\n3. when does a finding become a new question, and when\n   only a note on the page that found it?\n\n4. how many questions does one DIKW level hold before the list\n   is reviewed as a whole?\n\n5. a Knowledge question's needs are its premises, rivals and\n   test, and its judge is the conclusion: is three needs\n   enough there?",
   "originalText": "1. decided: the person signs each change, never the list\n\n2. must every question name a consumer before it is asked?\n\n3. when does a finding become a new question, and when\n   only a note on the page that found it?\n\n4. how many questions does one DIKW level hold before the list\n   is reviewed as a whole?\n\n5. a Knowledge question's needs are its premises, rivals and\n   test, and its judge is the conclusion: is three needs\n   enough there?",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "s-8daf99981798",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 6376,
   "y": 1578,
   "width": 1856.4,
   "height": 42.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": "s-f89f964fab01",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 66831707,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 9735541,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1791431790027,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1. A carried question keeps its words.   2. A question asks one thing, and its needs form a logic.   3. The review proposes keep, split, merge or move.\n4. A Data or Information ask states no cause.   5. A person signs every change; the old question is retired, never edited.   6. The shaper never reads results; the reviewer never reviews its own.",
   "originalText": "1. A carried question keeps its words.   2. A question asks one thing, and its needs form a logic.   3. The review proposes keep, split, merge or move.\n4. A Data or Information ask states no cause.   5. A person signs every change; the old question is retired, never edited.   6. The shaper never reads results; the reviewer never reviews its own.",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 8,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
